-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/123261ec-c24c-4516-b82a-dffd13657470
-- title:
--   Noisy gradient feedback and a run of Algorithm 3 (MA-AdaOGD)
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal G$ be a continuous game and $(\Omega,\mathcal M,\mathbb P)$ a probability space carrying the step-size draws of Algorithm 3. Write $\mathcal H_t=\sigma(x^t)\vee\sigma(\{\eta_i^s\}_{1\le i\le N,1\le s\le T})$ for the σ-algebra generated by the current joint action and all step sizes.
--
--   1. **Feedback.** For $1\le t\le T$, the observed noisy gradient $\xi^t$ is strongly measurable, $\xi^t$ and $\|\xi^t\|^2$ are integrable, and almost surely
--   $$
--   \mathbb E[\xi^t\mid\mathcal H_t]=v(x^t),\qquad \mathbb E[\|\xi^t\|^2\mid\mathcal H_t]\le G^2 .
--   $$
--   2. **Run.** From an initial point $x^1\in\mathcal X$, for $t=1,\dots,T$ and every agent $i$,
--   $$
--   x_i^{t+1}=\operatorname*{argmin}_{x_i\in\mathcal X_i}\Big\{(x_i-x_i^t)^\top\xi_i^t+\frac{\eta_i^{t+1}}{2}\|x_i-x_i^t\|^2\Big\},
--   $$
--   with $\eta_i^{t+1}$ the step size of line 6 of Algorithm 3.
--
--   This is the multi-agent adaptive online gradient descent of §3.2, run against the stochastic gradient oracle of §3.1.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The paper writes the feedback model as $\mathbb E[\xi^t\mid x^t]=v(x^t)$ and $\mathbb E[\|\xi^t\|^2\mid x^t]\le G^2$; here the conditioning is on $x^t$ together with all step sizes, which is the conditioning of the paper's proof (Appendix D, p.40). The noise may depend on the past beyond $x^t$. The argmin is stated sample by sample as "$x_i^{t+1}\in\mathcal X_i$ and its objective is at most the objective at every point of $\mathcal X_i$"; on a nonempty convex $\mathcal X_i$ the objective is strongly convex, so a minimizer, when it exists, is unique and the predicate determines the run.
-- source:
--   Jordan, Lin & Zhou, Adaptive, Doubly Optimal No-Regret Learning in Strongly Monotone and Exp-Concave Games with Gradient Feedback, arXiv:2310.14085v4, p.13 (feedback model, item 1); Algorithm 3, p.15; Appendix D, p.40 (the step sizes are generated independently of the feedback)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_AdaOGD_ContinuousGame
import Definitions.Def_AdaOGD_eta

namespace AdaOGD

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory
open scoped InnerProductSpace

variable {N : ℕ} {d : Fin N → ℕ}

/-- The σ-algebra generated by the current joint action `xᵗ` and all step sizes
`{ηˢᵢ}_{1≤i≤N, 1≤s≤T}`: the conditioning of the paper's feedback model in the proof of Lemma 3.10
(Jordan, Lin & Zhou, arXiv:2310.14085v4, Appendix D, p.40, "𝔼[· | xᵗ, {ηᵗᵢ}_{1≤i≤N,1≤t≤T}]"). -/
@[reducible] noncomputable def feedbackSigma {Ω : Type*} (M : Fin N → ℕ → Ω → ℕ) (T : ℕ)
    (x : ℕ → Ω → Joint d) (t : ℕ) : MeasurableSpace Ω :=
  MeasurableSpace.comap (x t) (borel (Joint d)) ⊔ etaSigma M T

/-- The noisy gradient feedback (arXiv:2310.14085v4, p.13, item 1): at each round `t` the observed
gradient `ξᵗ` is unbiased and bounded, `𝔼[ξᵗ | xᵗ] = v(xᵗ)` and `𝔼[‖ξᵗ‖² | xᵗ] ≤ G²`.

**Formalization Note** (Reading 1) The conditioning is on `xᵗ` together with all step sizes
`{ηˢᵢ}`, as in the paper's Appendix D, p.40: "{ηᵗᵢ} are generated independently of any noisy
gradient feedback, we have 𝔼[(x⋆ − xᵗ)ᵀξᵗ | xᵗ, {ηᵗᵢ}] = 𝔼[(x⋆ − xᵗ)ᵀv(xᵗ) | {ηᵗᵢ}],
𝔼[‖ξᵗ‖² | xᵗ, {ηᵗᵢ}] ≤ G²". The noise may depend on the past beyond `xᵗ`. `ξᵗ` is strongly
measurable and `ξᵗ`, `‖ξᵗ‖²` are integrable, so that both conditional expectations are defined;
along a run `xᵗ` is then measurable (`xᵗ⁺¹ᵢ` is the projection of `xᵗᵢ − ξᵗᵢ/ηᵗ⁺¹ᵢ` on `𝒳ᵢ`). The
conditions are imposed for `1 ≤ t ≤ T`, the rounds of Algorithm 3. -/
def IsOracle {Ω : Type*} {m0 : MeasurableSpace Ω} (G : ContinuousGame d) (P : Measure Ω) (T : ℕ)
    (Gc : ℝ) (M : Fin N → ℕ → Ω → ℕ) (x : ℕ → Ω → Joint d) (ξ : ℕ → Ω → Joint d) : Prop :=
  ∀ t : ℕ, 1 ≤ t → t ≤ T →
    StronglyMeasurable[m0] (ξ t) ∧
    Integrable (ξ t) P ∧
    Integrable (fun ω => ‖ξ t ω‖ ^ 2) P ∧
    P[ξ t | feedbackSigma M T x t] =ᵐ[P] (fun ω => G.v (x t ω)) ∧
    P[fun ω => ‖ξ t ω‖ ^ 2 | feedbackSigma M T x t] ≤ᵐ[P] (fun _ => Gc ^ 2)

/-- A run of Algorithm 3, MA-AdaOGD (arXiv:2310.14085v4, p.15): from the initial point
`x¹ = x1 ∈ 𝒳`, for `t = 1, …, T` and every agent `i`,
`xᵗ⁺¹ᵢ = argmin_{xᵢ ∈ 𝒳ᵢ} {(xᵢ − xᵗᵢ)ᵀξᵗᵢ + (ηᵗ⁺¹ᵢ/2)‖xᵢ − xᵗᵢ‖²}` (line 7), with the step size
`ηᵗ⁺¹ᵢ = (t + 1)/√(1 + max{M¹ᵢ, …, Mᵗᵢ})` of line 6 (`eta`).

**Formalization Note** The argmin is written as "`xᵗ⁺¹ᵢ ∈ 𝒳ᵢ` and its objective is at most the
objective at every `y ∈ 𝒳ᵢ`", sample by sample. On a nonempty convex compact `𝒳ᵢ` the objective is
strongly convex (`ηᵗ⁺¹ᵢ > 0`), so the minimizer exists and is unique and the predicate determines
the run. -/
def IsMAAdaOGDRun {Ω : Type*} (G : ContinuousGame d) (T : ℕ) (M : Fin N → ℕ → Ω → ℕ)
    (x1 : Joint d) (ξ : ℕ → Ω → Joint d) (x : ℕ → Ω → Joint d) : Prop :=
  x1 ∈ jointSet G.X ∧ (∀ ω, x 1 ω = x1) ∧
    ∀ t : ℕ, 1 ≤ t → t ≤ T → ∀ ω, ∀ i : Fin N,
      x (t + 1) ω i ∈ G.X i ∧
      ∀ y ∈ G.X i,
        ⟪x (t + 1) ω i - x t ω i, ξ t ω i⟫_ℝ + eta M i (t + 1) ω / 2 * ‖x (t + 1) ω i - x t ω i‖ ^ 2
          ≤ ⟪y - x t ω i, ξ t ω i⟫_ℝ + eta M i (t + 1) ω / 2 * ‖y - x t ω i‖ ^ 2

end AdaOGD


